Here, blow.

45
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,267
- Hey, aqualung.
(blowing nose)

46
00:01:55,267 --> 00:01:56,233
- Okay.

47
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:57,700
A little more, blow harder.

48
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:01,033
- [Magic Voice] Commercial
sign in five, four, three, two.

49
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:02,367
Commercial sign now.

50
00:02:02,367 --> 00:02:04,933
(coughing)
(sneezing)

51
00:02:04,933 --> 00:02:07,600
- Oh, we'll be right back.

52
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,200
(instrumental theme music)

53
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:14,067
(groaning)

54
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:15,800
- Oh, much better.

55
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,200
Whoa.
- Wow, yeah.

56
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:19,200
- Vapor action.
- It really works.

57
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:20,567
- Yeah, I feel great.

58
00:02:20,567 --> 00:02:22,833
Hey, what'd you put in
that vapor stuff anyway?

59
00:02:22,833 --> 00:02:26,900
- This says tetrahydrozoline,
sodium T-laurel sulfate,

60
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:31,900
UB40, FD&C Red 40, Simply Red,

61
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:35,000
flavor, magnesium
silicate, a flowing agent,

62
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,633
BHT to preserve
flavor, and Spacom.

63
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:39,967
It says may cause drowsiness,

64
00:02:39,967 --> 00:02:42,833
do not operate heavy machinery.

65
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:45,033
- Uh Joel, we are
heavy machinery, buddy.

66
00:02:45,033 --> 00:02:46,500
(laughing)
Cool, huh?

67
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,467
- Good one.

68
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:49,500
It says it may cause flashbacks.

69
00:02:50,667 --> 00:02:52,200
- Hey Joel, the mad
scientists are calling.

70
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,467
- Uh-oh.

71
00:02:53,467 --> 00:02:54,867
- He says, "That
was number five!"

72
00:02:54,867 --> 00:02:57,100
(laughing)

73
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:00,600
Oh, hello Joel.

74
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,433
Yard Ape here suggested you

75
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:05,200
go first on the
Invention Exchange.

76
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,833
Have at it, space guy.

77
00:03:07,833 --> 00:03:09,333
(laughing)

78
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:10,167
- Whoo!

79
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:13,600
- Ouch, jeepers.

80
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,667
Well, my invention this
week is for sign language.

81
00:03:16,667 --> 00:03:19,400
I don't know sign language,
so I invented this device.

82
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,833
It's a translator,
you speak into one end

83
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:24,100
and it does international
sign language on the other.

84
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,767
Let me show you what I mean.

85
00:03:25,767 --> 00:03:28,967
Okay, let's do something simple.

86
00:03:28,967 --> 00:03:30,567
I.

87
00:03:30,567 --> 00:03:31,600
See?

88
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:32,433
Love.

89
00:03:34,767 --> 00:03:36,000
You.

90
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,333
See how that works?

91
00:03:37,333 --> 00:03:38,600
- Aww, that's really sweet.
- That's great.

92
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,900
- And I also can do, I'd
like to do a little joke

93
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:45,433
for our friends who use sign
language who watch the show.

94
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,667
That's a number five!

95
00:03:47,667 --> 00:03:48,667
(chuckling)

96
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:50,100
It is kinda neat.

97
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,167
You can do a lot of
other things with it too,

98
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:53,300
like it's a hearing aid.

99
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:54,100
Hearing aid.

100
00:03:54,967 --> 00:03:56,333
(groaning)

101
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:57,633
Voice amplifier.

102
00:03:57,633 --> 00:03:59,367
Voice amplify.

103
00:03:59,367 --> 00:04:00,200
(chuckling)

104
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:02,467
And visor.

105
00:04:02,467 --> 00:04:03,300
- Huh, neat.

106
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,133
- See, pretty neat huh?

107
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:05,467
What do ya think, sirs?

108
00:04:05,467 --> 00:04:07,033
Straighten up.

109
00:04:07,033 --> 00:04:08,400
- What?

110
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,500
Your movie today, Joel, is--

111
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,767
- A biker film?

112
00:04:11,767 --> 00:04:13,467
- Biker film.

113
00:04:13,467 --> 00:04:14,900
Hey, how did you know that?

114
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,933
- Well, you're on bikes,
I just sorta guessed.

115
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:17,767
- No!

116
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,033
- No!

117
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:20,900
= No!

118
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:23,333
- No!

119
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:25,200
- No!

120
00:04:27,967 --> 00:04:29,267
- What are we saying no for?

121
00:04:29,267 --> 00:04:30,467
- I thought you knew.

122
00:04:30,467 --> 00:04:32,267
- I was following
your lead, mamajamma.

123
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:35,200
- Oh, well, send 'em
the movie then, Frank.

124
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,033
- I don't fink on soul brother.

125
00:04:37,033 --> 00:04:37,867
(alarms blaring)
- Ooh, movie sign!

126
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:43,033
(mechanical whirring)

127
00:04:50,333 --> 00:04:53,267
