255
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:55,100
- [Tom] They're cops.

256
00:08:56,867 --> 00:08:59,233
- [Crow] Hey, Eric Lindberg,
he flew from New York to Paris.

257
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:00,600
- [Joel] Would you shut up?

258
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,100
♪ Shocking everyone they meet ♪

259
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:04,733
- [Crow] Motorcycles
by Ford Puckett,

260
00:09:04,733 --> 00:09:06,033
Kirby Puckett's brother.

261
00:09:06,033 --> 00:09:07,133
(chuckling)

262
00:09:07,133 --> 00:09:09,567
- [Joel] Just stop.

263
00:09:09,567 --> 00:09:10,967
- [Crow] Hey Bill,
your rear's done.

264
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,200
(laughing)

265
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,933
- [Joel] Ah jeez, that's
cool, I can dig that.

266
00:09:14,933 --> 00:09:17,033
♪ Hellcats, parading
down the street ♪

267
00:09:17,033 --> 00:09:18,133
- [Joel] Even if we disagree,

268
00:09:18,133 --> 00:09:19,500
it's all in good-natured
fun isn't it?

269
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:20,900
- [Tom] Yeah, it sure is.

270
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,600
- [Crow] Cemetery
furnishings by Jiffy Tomb.

271
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,800
- [Tom] Negative cutter,
he says "Oh, I hate my job.

272
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,233
"Everything about it is bad."

273
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,700
♪ Don't mess around ♪

274
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,433
- [Crow] Author of
the Kinzie report.

275
00:09:29,433 --> 00:09:30,600
♪ Hellcats ♪

276
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,100
- [Crow] Fine
Corinthian leather.

277
00:09:32,100 --> 00:09:34,233
- [Tom] Cordoza.
(chuckling)

278
00:09:34,233 --> 00:09:35,400
♪ Hellcats ♪
- [Joel] Oh, if this is

279
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,867
a Slatzer film, it
might get really bloody.

280
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:39,067
- [Crow] That's slasher.

281
00:09:39,933 --> 00:09:41,867
♪ Hellcats ♪

282
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:44,033
- [Tom] Scenic Love Canal.

283
00:09:44,033 --> 00:09:46,800
(engine revving)

284
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:49,267
- [Joel] Wow.
(funky music)

285
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:53,400
- [Tom] Hey, they're playing
The Girl from Ipanema here.

286
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:55,467
- [Joel] Long and cool
and tan and lovely,

287
00:09:55,467 --> 00:09:57,800
the boy from
Ipanema goes biking,

288
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,200
and when he bikes, all the guys

289
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:01,333
on their motor trikes go "Ah."

290
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,367
- [Tom] Hellcats, terrorizing
the desolate wastelands

291
00:10:05,367 --> 00:10:07,533
for over half a century.

292
00:10:07,533 --> 00:10:09,100
Man welded to machine.

293
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,133
- [Crow] Hey, fancy
meeting you here.

294
00:10:17,033 --> 00:10:19,967
(suspenseful music)

295
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:22,200
- [Joel] Hmm, still a bike.

296
00:10:23,067 --> 00:10:25,867
(Tom humming)

297
00:10:25,867 --> 00:10:27,033
- [Crow] Here's
your modeling clay.

298
00:10:27,033 --> 00:10:27,867
I made a bunny.

299
00:10:29,133 --> 00:10:30,333
- [Tom] Oh, smart.

300
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:31,533
They're in the
middle of nowhere,

301
00:10:31,533 --> 00:10:32,767
but they make their drug
deal out in the open

302
00:10:32,767 --> 00:10:34,900
by the side of the road
while a car passes by!

303
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:37,000
- [Joel] Why do you
think they call it dope?

304
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,100
(engines revving)

305
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,633
- [Crow] Remember, we
got bridge club at 4:00.

306
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:42,433
- [Joel] Yep.

307
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:44,633
Yeah, this thing'll...

308
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:46,433
I get on this and

309
00:10:46,433 --> 00:10:47,433
the wheels...

310
00:10:49,133 --> 00:10:50,800
- [Tom] I know this wiener dude,

311
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,533
he sells this wiener food.

312
00:10:52,533 --> 00:10:55,533
He gives me everything from
tire irons on down, hey.

313
00:10:55,533 --> 00:10:58,367
I'd like to split his head
open with a tire iron.

314
00:10:58,367 --> 00:10:59,633
Heh, I made that up myself.

315
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:00,567
- [Joel] Yeah.
- [Crow] That's great.

316
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:01,767
(chuckling)

317
00:11:01,767 --> 00:11:03,033
Hey, his two-cycle's got some

318
00:11:03,033 --> 00:11:04,967
real knocking and
pinging problems.

319
00:11:07,967 --> 00:11:10,367
- [Tom] Now I just turn
right at the slag heap.

320
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:11,233
- [Joel] Yeah.

321
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:13,933
Must be on the way home.

322
00:11:13,933 --> 00:11:15,867
Yeah, looks like
nice digs, you know.

323
00:11:15,867 --> 00:11:17,700
It's not much, but
it's centrally located.

324
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:19,900
No kids cutting across
the lawn or anything.

325
00:11:21,267 --> 00:11:23,467
Hey old lady, I'm home.

326
00:11:23,467 --> 00:11:24,667
- You been on a
tour or something?

327
00:11:24,667 --> 00:11:26,433
I've been waiting here
for over two hours

328
00:11:26,433 --> 00:11:28,033
and Adrian's gonna
be madder than hell.

329
00:11:28,033 --> 00:11:28,967
- [Tom] Oooh.

330
00:11:28,967 --> 00:11:30,867
- Here's the money I made.

331
00:11:30,867 --> 00:11:32,600
Snake was late
running in from Mexico

332
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,400
and I couldn't
afford to get caught

333
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,967
with that powder in my pocket.

334
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:38,100
- [Crow] (chuckling)
Nice read, Richards.

335
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:43,433
- [Joel] I'm a stranger
to my own soul.

336
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:47,633
(engine starting)

337
00:11:48,867 --> 00:11:49,967
Listen, there's a
dance next Friday

338
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:51,100
and I was thinking maybe--

339
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:52,333
Oh, forget it.

340
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:54,133
- [Tom] Wonder if
she got her bra back.

341
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,533
- [Crow] Hey, I
remember her now.

342
00:11:58,533 --> 00:12:00,167
She was the star of
Then Came Bronson.

343
00:12:00,167 --> 00:12:01,767
- [Joel] That was a guy.
- [Crow] No it wasn't

344
00:12:01,767 --> 00:12:03,167
- [Joel] It was too.
- [Crow] Was not.

345
00:12:03,167 --> 00:12:04,767
- [Tom] Was Not Was, there.

346
00:12:04,767 --> 00:12:06,367
I made a meaningless
pop culture reference,

347
00:12:06,367 --> 00:12:07,667
now knock it off!

348
00:12:09,467 --> 00:12:10,733
- [Crow] Well where's
she going anyway?

349
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:12,633
- [Joel] I don't know,
nowhere in particular.

350
00:12:12,633 --> 00:12:14,400
- [Crow] Man, I sure envy her.

351
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,000
- [Joel] Yeah
well, take it easy.

352
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,367
- [Tom] For those of you
playing along at home,

353
00:12:17,367 --> 00:12:19,667
Joel and Crow just
reenacted the opening scene

354
00:12:19,667 --> 00:12:21,000
of Then Came Bronson.

355
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
We'll be right back.

356
00:12:29,867 --> 00:12:32,333
(laughing)

357
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:33,500
- You're late.

358
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,833
- [Tom] Don Fido is mad.

359
00:12:35,733 --> 00:12:37,700
- I don't like waiting.

360
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:40,367
What do you hear from the
good Detective Chapman?

361
00:12:40,367 --> 00:12:41,633
- He's got us up tight.

362
00:12:44,267 --> 00:12:47,267
- In that case, we'll
have to loosen things up.

363
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:48,467
(loud music chord)
- [Joel] I'm the director,

364
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:50,433
I make the music
louder when it's on me.

365
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,967
- [Crow] All done?

366
00:12:56,967 --> 00:12:58,833
Shep, some day this
will all be yours.

367
00:12:58,833 --> 00:13:00,667
- [Tom] What a neat bunch.

368
00:13:00,667 --> 00:13:01,600
We'll be right back.

369
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:05,067
(instrumental theme music)

370
00:13:10,067 --> 00:13:11,000
(dramatic music)

371
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,600
- [Joel] Meanwhile on Route 66,

372
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:14,733
James Dean takes a lazy spin.

373
00:13:14,733 --> 00:13:17,233
- [Tom] What's in store for
these two lamebrains here?

374
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:18,700
- [Crow] I said I'm pregnant!

375
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:23,600
- [Tom] Oh, I just love
this Charles Ives music.

376
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,167
Got any Ralph Vaughan Williams?

377
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:31,867
- [Joel] It's me, the director
again, I use my talents.

378
00:13:33,933 --> 00:13:35,567
- [Tom] Tony Houston,
co-writer and AD.

379
00:13:35,567 --> 00:13:36,500
I got the dry look.

380
00:13:40,467 --> 00:13:42,867
- [Crow] Let's park the
Barbiemobile right here.

381
00:13:47,067 --> 00:13:49,433
- [Tom] Let's part the
Gangstermobile right here.

382
00:13:51,933 --> 00:13:54,067
(Tom humming)

383
00:13:54,067 --> 00:13:55,633
- [Joel] I need it now.

384
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:56,467
- [Tom] Now, now!

385
00:13:59,267 --> 00:14:00,500
- [Crow] Hmm?

386
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:01,933
Hey, Bob.

387
00:14:01,933 --> 00:14:03,733
That's me up there.

388
00:14:03,733 --> 00:14:05,233
(soft music)

389
00:14:05,233 --> 00:14:09,433
- [Joel] Take my hand, I'm
a stranger in paradise.

390
00:14:09,433 --> 00:14:12,733
[Crow] She's wearing a
Sunkist promotional pantsuit.

391
00:14:12,733 --> 00:14:14,333
Must be one of the gold diggers.

392
00:14:17,300 --> 00:14:20,167
- [Tom] Oh boy,
what a tough lie.

393
00:14:20,167 --> 00:14:22,267
I'm glad I brought my light bag.

394
00:14:22,267 --> 00:14:24,167
I was playing a Wilson four.

395
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:26,167
- [Crow] Steve has a problem.

396
00:14:26,167 --> 00:14:27,800
His problem is down there.

397
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,833
Now he must tell Eliza.

398
00:14:29,833 --> 00:14:30,667
- Tell me.

399
00:14:31,867 --> 00:14:33,333
- [Joel] I was in Guam

400
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:34,633
and they stuck bamboo
under my nails, all right?

401
00:14:34,633 --> 00:14:36,300
- You broke your promise.

402
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:39,633
Quote, "Let's take a long
drive in the country."

403
00:14:39,633 --> 00:14:40,867
- [All] Unquote.

404
00:14:40,867 --> 00:14:42,467
- "Maybe the fresh air
will clear my head.

405
00:14:42,467 --> 00:14:45,733
"I'm beginning to feel more
like a junkie than a narco cop."

406
00:14:45,733 --> 00:14:47,100
- [Joel] You're not
supposed to take them,

407
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:48,367
just confiscate 'em.

408
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:50,900
- Yellow jackets,
reds, bennies, H.

409
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:52,400
- Look--

410
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:54,100
- [Crow] Why do you think
they call it exposition?

411
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,833
- With a cigarette?

412
00:14:55,833 --> 00:14:57,300
- They're in the car.

413
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:58,200
- [Tom] Hey, he's the guy from
the beginning of the film,

414
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,400
Detective Plot Point.

415
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:00,767
- What I go through.

416
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:03,800
- [Tom] D'oh.

417
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:05,033
- [Joel] And get me a slug from

418
00:15:05,033 --> 00:15:06,967
a thirty-aught-six
when you're up.

419
00:15:06,967 --> 00:15:09,567
(suspenseful music)

420
00:15:09,567 --> 00:15:11,067
- [Tom] Hey...

421
00:15:11,067 --> 00:15:13,433
Hey, I remember this from
The Day of the Jackal, guys.

422
00:15:17,033 --> 00:15:19,300
- [Crow] And now, Red
in the silent spot.

423
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:21,433
Red plays a guy about
to get gunned down.

424
00:15:21,433 --> 00:15:22,900
Let's watch.

425
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:24,767
- [Joel] Found this in
a warehouse in Dallas,

426
00:15:24,767 --> 00:15:25,967
I hope it works.

427
00:15:25,967 --> 00:15:27,800
- [Tom] You gettin'
this, Zapruder?

428
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,633
There.

429
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:32,633
(gun fires)

430
00:15:32,633 --> 00:15:33,467
Huh?

431
00:15:36,500 --> 00:15:37,833
- [Crow] Oh, that
sounds like Steve

432
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,733
taking a slug from
a thirty-aught-six.

433
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,867
- [Tom] Steve's dead now.

434
00:15:41,867 --> 00:15:43,200
From here on in, Steve's death

435
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:45,433
will be represented by the oboe.

436
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:49,967
- [Joel] Oh, what a time to
dress wrong for a slaying.

437
00:15:49,967 --> 00:15:52,300
- [Tom] It's not like
Steve to run off and die.

438
00:15:53,967 --> 00:15:55,667
(screaming)
- No!

439
00:15:55,667 --> 00:15:57,133
- [Joel] My seat covers!

440
00:15:57,133 --> 00:15:59,033
(screaming)

441
00:15:59,033 --> 00:16:00,467
- [Tom] Nice screams.

442
00:16:00,467 --> 00:16:03,400
- [Crow] Meanwhile,
in Gordon Gekko's jet.

443
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,667
(grunting)

444
00:16:06,833 --> 00:16:08,700
- [Joel] Ah, so
that's how it works.

445
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,533
All right.

446
00:16:10,467 --> 00:16:11,900
- [Tom] Ross Hagen! (groaning)

447
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:13,333
- [Joel] Oh man.

448
00:16:13,333 --> 00:16:14,867
Captain Ross Hagen to you, pal.

449
00:16:21,633 --> 00:16:23,133
- Thanks for the ride.

450
00:16:23,133 --> 00:16:24,633
- We owe you much
more than a ride, son.

451
00:16:24,633 --> 00:16:26,133
- [Crow] You're a way of life.

452
00:16:31,767 --> 00:16:32,733
- [Joel] Hey Steve, mind if we

453
00:16:32,733 --> 00:16:34,400
get in on some of that action?

454
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,033
- Senator Carter,
Senator Linfield,

455
00:16:36,033 --> 00:16:38,100
this is my brother's
fiancee, Linda Martin.

456
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,200
- My pleasure, Ms. Martin.

457
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,400
- [Crow] Ah, so she's available?

458
00:16:40,400 --> 00:16:42,400
- Sergeant Chapman
told us what happened.

459
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:45,367
You have the deepest
sympathy of both myself and--

460
00:16:45,367 --> 00:16:47,967
- [Joel] The entire human
race, including red China.

461
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:54,567
- [Crow] Thanks for the jet.

462
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:57,833
- [Joel] You know,
these are great lyrics.

463
00:16:57,833 --> 00:16:59,100
You've got real talent!

464
00:16:59,100 --> 00:17:01,767
- That's it, all Dave
had was the notebook.

465
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,500
- No names, no faces,
you never saw anyone.

466
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:07,300
- [Tom] Just
elbows, it was dark.

467
00:17:10,933 --> 00:17:12,433
- Hellcats.

468
00:17:12,433 --> 00:17:13,567
(Tom humming theme song)

469
00:17:13,567 --> 00:17:14,833
- I wonder.
- [Linda] What?

470
00:17:14,833 --> 00:17:16,033
- [Crow] Who wrote
the book of love?

471
00:17:16,033 --> 00:17:19,100
- If you hunt them
like you hunt people.

472
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:20,300
- [Joel] Yeah, you kinda do.

473
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,400
Dig a two-foot hole,
put Crisco in--

474
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,400
Oh, that's bears.

475
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:24,900
- [Crow] Uh, that's the closet.

476
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,133
- What are you planning to do?

477
00:17:26,133 --> 00:17:27,400
- [Joel] Catch a
show at the Copa.

478
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:28,967
Whenever a brother dies,
they fly me in for free.

479
00:17:28,967 --> 00:17:30,367
I like to take advantage.

480
00:17:34,733 --> 00:17:39,467
- [Crow] Uh, Ross, you're
wearing her purse on your head.

481
00:17:40,900 --> 00:17:42,833
- [Tom] I dare you to knock
this battery off my shoulder.

482
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:46,567
Go ahead, I dare ya.

483
00:17:46,567 --> 00:17:50,167
- [Joel] Utah, I can't
believe I'm still in Utah.

484
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:55,833
I'm filled with shame, I am.

485
00:17:58,967 --> 00:18:01,733
(engine revving)

486
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,300
- [Crow] Then came moron.

487
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,533
(squeaking)

488
00:18:11,533 --> 00:18:14,433
(indistinct singing)

489
00:18:14,433 --> 00:18:15,633
- [Tom] Great song, huh?

490
00:18:17,067 --> 00:18:18,700
Hi, I'm Shelly. (giggling)

491
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:19,800
Rub my belly.

492
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:28,700
- [Crow] Today's tough
but tender youth,

493
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:31,133
driving the big steamers
across this great land.

494
00:18:31,133 --> 00:18:33,667
- [Tom] Whoa, whoa, whoa.

495
00:18:33,667 --> 00:18:35,567
Filmed in Zapruder-vision, guys.

496
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:42,133
(imitating singer)

497
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,100
- [Joel] Innuendo freeway.

498
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:49,033
- [Crow] Yeah, you don't have to

499
00:18:49,033 --> 00:18:50,500
be Fellini to figure that out.

500
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,833
(chuckling)

501
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,533
- [Crow] What's the point?

502
00:18:59,533 --> 00:19:01,667
- [Tom] Yeah, I bet if the
scientists sent us Citizen Kane,

503
00:19:01,667 --> 00:19:04,233
it'd have a 20-minute
sled sequence in it.

504
00:19:05,867 --> 00:19:07,167
- [Crow] Hey Joel,
what are these films

505
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:08,633
trying to teach us about life?

506
00:19:08,633 --> 00:19:10,067
- [Joel] Well I guess
they're trying to say that

507
00:19:10,067 --> 00:19:12,533
if we're born, and then we die

508
00:19:12,533 --> 00:19:14,333
and there's lots of
padding in between.

509
00:19:14,333 --> 00:19:15,333
- [Crow] Oh.

510
00:19:18,433 --> 00:19:19,900
- [Tom] Focus.

511
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:21,167
- [Crow] Oh, couldn't they
just have ordered out?

512
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:22,400
That's a long way
to go for a taco.

513
00:19:23,967 --> 00:19:25,300
- [Joel] Oh, wrong place.

514
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:26,867
We better start cruising again.

515
00:19:26,867 --> 00:19:28,767
(humming)

516
00:19:28,767 --> 00:19:30,500
- Go for the throat.

517
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:32,400
- [Tom] Uh, maybe you should
clear your throat first.

518
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:36,300
- [Joel] Hmm, Moonfire Inn, huh?

519
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:39,233
Looks like a nice country inn,
maybe we'll see Bob Newhart.

520
00:19:41,733 --> 00:19:42,667
- [Tom] Whoa!

521
00:19:42,667 --> 00:19:44,267
What happened to his head?

522
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:45,500
- [Crow] Oh, Linda Blair.

523
00:19:46,933 --> 00:19:51,067
- [Tom] Oh, making a ship model.

524
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,400
Ah men, enjoying
their manliness.

525
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,667
(grunting)

526
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:05,567
- [Crow] Excuse
me, that's illegal.

527
00:20:05,567 --> 00:20:09,433
- Oh well, high ho.

528
00:20:09,433 --> 00:20:10,500
- [Tom] What is he, a dwarf?

529
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,000
- Come to Little Daddy, do.

530
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,433
- Back off, Six Pack.

531
00:20:13,433 --> 00:20:15,767
It's too early
and I'm too sober.

532
00:20:15,767 --> 00:20:17,100
- [Crow] And my voice
is dubbed incorrectly.

533
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:18,800
- I'm drunk enough
for both of us.

534
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:23,333
You know I always like to
start things off with a bang.

535
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:25,100
(Tom mumbling)

536
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,733
- Get her, Pack!

537
00:20:26,733 --> 00:20:29,200
- [Joel] Eww.

538
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,300
- Okay, baby.

539
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:32,733
- [Joel] I don't
mind telling you,

540
00:20:32,733 --> 00:20:34,367
he looks a lot like
Gilbert Gottfried.

541
00:20:37,533 --> 00:20:38,367
Huh?

542
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:39,433
- [Crow] Oh...

543
00:20:39,433 --> 00:20:43,300
(imitating sad trombone music)

544
00:20:45,033 --> 00:20:47,667
- I didn't see you, man.

545
00:20:47,667 --> 00:20:48,633
Let me buy you a beer.

546
00:20:48,633 --> 00:20:49,833
- [Tom] Uh, you just did.

547
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:53,633
- [Joel] Ah, let me get
out of some of these

548
00:20:53,633 --> 00:20:55,500
wet clothes and
into a dry martini.

549
00:20:57,767 --> 00:20:58,733
- [Crow] Who does
your decorating,

550
00:20:58,733 --> 00:21:00,067
Paul Revere and the Raiders?

551
00:21:01,767 --> 00:21:04,000
- [Joel] I'm bemused by charmed
by this plucky stranger.

552
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,100
- [Tom] I resent him.

553
00:21:08,633 --> 00:21:11,400
- [Crow] Oh, it's a book
signing party for 150 Sex.

554
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,900
(chuckling)

555
00:21:12,900 --> 00:21:14,133
- [Tom] Looks like Jim Garner

556
00:21:14,133 --> 00:21:16,467
poked out Mariette
Hartley's eye there.

557
00:21:16,467 --> 00:21:19,067
- [Joel] Hey, what's my
motivation in this scene?

558
00:21:19,067 --> 00:21:19,900
Okay, got it.

559
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:24,133
- Hey you, where you from?

560
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:26,167
- [Tom] Sidehackers.

561
00:21:26,167 --> 00:21:27,867
- My name's Gordon.

562
00:21:27,867 --> 00:21:29,600
- That's cute, man, real cute.

563
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:30,567
- [Crow] Thank you.

564
00:21:30,567 --> 00:21:31,967
- I asked you where you're from.

565
00:21:31,967 --> 00:21:35,133
- I said north.
- You flying colors?

566
00:21:35,133 --> 00:21:36,600
- Man, we've been
busted so many times

567
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:39,333
the only colors I fly
are exhaust black.

568
00:21:39,333 --> 00:21:40,967
- I never could
run with a loser.

569
00:21:42,833 --> 00:21:45,200
- [Joel] What are
we talking about?

570
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,667
- This is the main mama.

571
00:21:47,733 --> 00:21:49,000
- You hot?

572
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,533
- [Tom] Aw, it's
just the humidity.

573
00:21:51,467 --> 00:21:53,400
(mumbling)

574
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:55,867
- You take your old lady
on that hog and you move.

575
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:58,300
I tell the blue.

576
00:21:58,300 --> 00:21:59,733
- [Crow] What the
heck are they saying?

577
00:21:59,733 --> 00:22:02,100
It's like he's speaking
in an ancient tongue.

578
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:04,267
- And he said "not
here, you don't."

579
00:22:04,267 --> 00:22:06,367
And he smacked me five
times on the wrist.

580
00:22:06,367 --> 00:22:09,333
- [Joel] Ah, he went to a
Catholic school, probably.

581
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:11,067
(bots agreeing)

582
00:22:11,067 --> 00:22:12,867
- You sound like a preacher.

583
00:22:12,867 --> 00:22:14,967
(chuckling)
- Yeah, all mouth.

584
00:22:18,467 --> 00:22:20,067
- [Tom] Oh, he's a pushover.

585
00:22:21,633 --> 00:22:23,133
- [Crow] He's no fun,
he fell right over.

586
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:24,633
- [Tom] (chuckling) Thank you.

587
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:29,033
- [Crow] Hey, you almost
spilled my Shamrock Shake.

588
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,400
- You hit Daddy.
- [Joel] He hit Big Jake.

589
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:40,833
- [Tom] I've got my eye on you.

590
00:22:43,433 --> 00:22:44,333
- Back off.

591
00:22:45,833 --> 00:22:47,733
- [Joel] We better
back off ourselves.

592
00:22:47,733 --> 00:22:48,967
Let's go, you guys.

593
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,633
- [Tom] What are
these people saying?

594
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:53,300
- How 'bout a couple
more beers, Lem?

595
00:22:53,300 --> 00:22:55,433
(mechanical whirring)

596
00:22:55,433 --> 00:22:58,067
(doors closing)

597
00:23:04,867 --> 00:23:05,833
- Let's see here.

598
00:23:05,833 --> 00:23:09,500
Dear diary, call me Ishmael.

599
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:10,667
(chuckling) Just kidding.

600
00:23:10,667 --> 00:23:11,500
Let's try that again.

601
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,933
Dear diary, June 10th.

602
00:23:12,933 --> 00:23:15,400
This day started
strange when Crow and I

603
00:23:15,400 --> 00:23:18,933
got into a fight in the
load pan bay, period.

604
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:21,700
It all started when,
unprovoked, Crow called me

605
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:24,900
a, quote, "sweatbeetle
dickweed," end quote, period.

606
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,933
Then all of a
sudden, he jumped me

607
00:23:26,933 --> 00:23:29,767
and the next thing I
know, I was winning

608
00:23:29,767 --> 00:23:31,333
when Joel discovered us.

609
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:34,367
He had to steam-hose us
off, it was a real mess,

610
00:23:34,367 --> 00:23:36,567
period, paragraph there.

611
00:23:37,533 --> 00:23:38,500
Damn electric typewriters.

612
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,733
Oh, okay, here we go.

613
00:23:39,733 --> 00:23:41,600
Joel says when Crow
and I get into fights,

614
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:43,433
even if it isn't my
fault, we should remember

615
00:23:43,433 --> 00:23:46,133
the good times we had together.

616
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:48,900
Like the other day, or
maybe it was last year.

617
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:50,167
Uh, before my voice changed.

618
00:23:50,167 --> 00:23:52,467
Cambot, would you serve
that up for us, please?

619
00:23:52,467 --> 00:23:53,400
(eerie music)

620
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,033
Perhaps it was two weeks ago...

621
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:59,933
- Must get back
to Galileo Seven.

622
00:23:59,933 --> 00:24:03,567
Lives of 400 crew
members hang in balance!

623
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,567
- Vision fading.

624
00:24:06,567 --> 00:24:09,933
Must cut transponder from wrist,

625
00:24:09,933 --> 00:24:13,233
fashion crude phaser device
with bed slat and light bulb.

626
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:16,333
- Must control myself,

627
00:24:16,333 --> 00:24:19,600
must find pastel-colored
native female.

628
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,800
Execute prime directive, ahhh!

629
00:24:21,800 --> 00:24:23,300
(choking)

630
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:25,633
- Handsúso young-looking.

631
00:24:25,633 --> 00:24:27,867
Mrs. Berg, I thought
you were Dale.

632
00:24:27,867 --> 00:24:29,433
(groaning)

633
00:24:29,433 --> 00:24:32,400
- Throat scratchy, hands so dry

634
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:33,867
can scratch name into--

635
00:24:33,867 --> 00:24:35,767
(groaning)

636
00:24:35,767 --> 00:24:39,467
- Embarrassing cuticles
on fingernails.

637
00:24:39,467 --> 00:24:41,000
Must utilize emotional memory--

638
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,733
- Ah, listen Servo,
stop it, stop it.

639
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:44,900
- Stop?
- No, uh-uh.

640
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,400
- That was my big scene, Joel!

641
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,700
- Yeah, we were just
getting into it.

642
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:48,967
- This just isn't working.

643
00:24:48,967 --> 00:24:51,100
I don't know how Shatner
does it week after week.

644
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:53,367
- I don't know why he does
it or who lets him do it.

645
00:24:53,367 --> 00:24:55,233
- I think we should
just be glad he does it.

646
00:24:55,233 --> 00:24:57,533
(eerie music)

647
00:24:57,533 --> 00:24:58,633
Three months--

648
00:24:58,633 --> 00:25:00,500
Ah, we'll be right back.

649
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:01,400
Okay, I got it.

650
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:03,333
It was a fortnight ago,

651
00:25:06,467 --> 00:25:11,467
and it was a, hey, a
dark and stormy night!

652
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:13,000
(chuckling)

653
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,567
(instrumental theme music)

654
00:25:22,467 --> 00:25:24,067
- [Joel] Hey, what were
you doing in there anyway?

655
00:25:24,067 --> 00:25:25,567
- [Tom] Oh, not
much, just typing.

656
00:25:25,567 --> 00:25:26,800
Cambot gave me a neat flashback.

657
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,300
- [Joel] Oh.

658
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:29,667
- Mama, she's got
whooping cough.

659
00:25:29,667 --> 00:25:31,300
- Sick?

660
00:25:31,300 --> 00:25:33,367
- [Crow] I doubt it.
- I'll take a look at her.

661
00:25:33,367 --> 00:25:35,200
- Appreciate it.

662
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:36,833
- [Joel] You want
me to go right now?

663
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:37,667
I will.

664
00:25:41,767 --> 00:25:43,467
Nice guy, kinda funny.

665
00:25:43,467 --> 00:25:44,867
- [Tom] You know, those glasses

666
00:25:44,867 --> 00:25:47,300
just don't disguise the receding
hairline there, do they?

667
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:49,000
- [Joel] He drew eyes up on top.

668
00:25:50,167 --> 00:25:52,567
- [Crow] Looks like
an unsavory character.

669
00:25:52,567 --> 00:25:53,600
I can't have any of that.

670
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:55,533
I'd better call Plot Stoppers.

671
00:25:58,900 --> 00:26:00,133
- [Joel] Hello, angels.

672
00:26:00,133 --> 00:26:01,367
- [Adrian] Good boy.

673
00:26:01,367 --> 00:26:03,967
Information never hurts, Jack.

674
00:26:03,967 --> 00:26:05,433
Keep 'em open.

675
00:26:05,433 --> 00:26:06,500
(sultry music)

676
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:08,033
Goldie?

677
00:26:08,033 --> 00:26:10,033
- [Joel] That reminds me,
I must get my watch fixed.

678
00:26:10,033 --> 00:26:11,500
- [Tom] Mom!?

679
00:26:11,500 --> 00:26:13,567
- How's Tahiti sound?

680
00:26:13,567 --> 00:26:16,600
- Mmm.
- I thought you'd like it.

681
00:26:18,367 --> 00:26:19,867
(groaning)

682
00:26:19,867 --> 00:26:21,400
- [Crow] Her back looks
like a Klingon's forehead.

683
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:23,533
- Time to move on?

684
00:26:23,533 --> 00:26:25,033
- [Joel] What do you call that?

685
00:26:25,900 --> 00:26:27,067
- [Crow] Illegal?

686
00:26:27,067 --> 00:26:28,833
- [Joel] Lunch
coming up. (gagging)

687
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:31,000
(yelling)

688
00:26:35,333 --> 00:26:36,533
- [Tom] Looks like
every selection there

689
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:38,733
is Louie, Louie
except for this one.

690
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:40,933
(upbeat music)

691
00:26:40,933 --> 00:26:42,767
This is the Question Mark
before the Mysterions.

692
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:43,967
♪ I go out when
the mood is right ♪

693
00:26:43,967 --> 00:26:45,767
- [Joel] did you
know this cameraman

694
00:26:45,767 --> 00:26:47,467
got his first job
on Midnight Special?

695
00:26:47,467 --> 00:26:50,033
- [Crow] Hey, Louise Lasser.

696
00:26:50,033 --> 00:26:54,300
♪ And then I take
my baby's hand ♪

697
00:26:54,300 --> 00:26:56,500
- [Tom] Suzy, dead at 21.

698
00:26:56,500 --> 00:26:59,400
♪ 'Cause I can't take a chance ♪

699
00:26:59,400 --> 00:27:02,667
- [Joel] Kipper, sells
lightly salted meat products.

700
00:27:02,667 --> 00:27:06,333
- [Crow] Six Pack, currently
working for Roseanne Barr Show.

701
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:07,533
♪ On losing my baby ♪
- [Tom] Little Sally,

702
00:27:07,533 --> 00:27:09,200
girl friday to
Susan Saint James.

703
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:11,700
- [Crow] Slugger, found dead

704
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:13,433
with Coors Party Ball
lodged in throat.

705
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:15,700
- [Joel] Spazzy, broken neck

706
00:27:15,700 --> 00:27:17,800
shortly after filming
of this movie.

707
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:21,100
- [Tom] Puck, co-founder of
the avant-garde dance group.

708
00:27:21,100 --> 00:27:22,633
- [Crow] Iggy Pop,
we don't know why.

709
00:27:22,633 --> 00:27:23,767
- [Joel] And Patches.

710
00:27:24,967 --> 00:27:26,333
- [Tom] Squatter, took
a baseball in the head

711
00:27:26,333 --> 00:27:28,433
in the third inning
at an Angels game.

712
00:27:31,100 --> 00:27:32,400
- [Joel] Ewww!
- [Crow] I hope that's beer!

713
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:33,567
- [Tom] Yikes!

714
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,467
- [Joel] Hey, it's
Shields and Yarnell

715
00:27:37,467 --> 00:27:41,133
working a crowd with their
famous sidewalk robot routine.

716
00:27:41,133 --> 00:27:42,067
- [Tom] I can't stop doing this,

717
00:27:42,067 --> 00:27:43,533
you think I like doing this?

718
00:27:43,533 --> 00:27:44,467
I can't stop.

719
00:27:44,467 --> 00:27:45,700
- [Crow] That was number nine!

720
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:47,800
(hooting)

721
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:49,000
- [Joel] Somebody put a wallet

722
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,533
under the guy's
tongue or something.

723
00:27:51,833 --> 00:27:53,400
- [Tom] Bad, bad girl, naughty.

724
00:27:54,567 --> 00:27:56,033
- [Crow] Timothy Hutton,
before the boat trip.

725
00:27:56,033 --> 00:27:57,500
(chuckling)

726
00:27:57,500 --> 00:28:01,167
- [Joel] Shagster, camouflage
expert, can hide anywhere.

727
00:28:01,167 --> 00:28:05,167
And there's more, there's
Jingo and Baby Burlap

728
00:28:05,167 --> 00:28:08,933
and Fleagle and Beagle
and Drooper and Snork,

729
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:12,133
and uh-oh, it's the stinky guy.

730
00:28:13,800 --> 00:28:15,100
- [Tom] Drew Barrymore.

731
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:18,100
♪ I send her letters
almost every day ♪

732
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:21,733
♪ So she'll never go astray ♪

733
00:28:21,733 --> 00:28:23,200
- [Crow] And aman
so mean he once

734
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:25,433
shot himself just
for snoring too loud.

735
00:28:25,433 --> 00:28:27,600
♪ Make sure that
she's right at home ♪

736
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:28,800
- [Tom] Sally Kellerman!

737
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:30,400
Whoa, lookin' hot.

738
00:28:31,333 --> 00:28:32,833
♪ On losin' my baby ♪

739
00:28:32,833 --> 00:28:34,000
- [Crow] Well, I gotta admit it.

740
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,567
It does look like a fun party

741
00:28:35,567 --> 00:28:37,900
♪ I can't take a chance ♪

742
00:28:37,900 --> 00:28:41,000
♪ I'm losing my baby ♪

743
00:28:43,100 --> 00:28:44,167
- [Joel] Hey!

744
00:28:45,833 --> 00:28:47,567
Oh mama, Santa's home.

745
00:28:49,067 --> 00:28:50,333
- [Crow] More, more
of the old guy!

746
00:28:50,333 --> 00:28:51,567
Whoo!

747
00:28:51,567 --> 00:28:52,400
♪ I don't want to
take a chance ♪

748
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:53,567
♪ To leave you behind ♪

749
00:28:53,567 --> 00:28:55,167
- [Tom] There's
Trembler and Wheezer.

750
00:28:56,867 --> 00:28:59,600
♪ I go out when
the moon is right ♪

751
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:00,900
- [Joel] That's sweet.

752
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:02,367
♪ And the stars are
shinin' bright ♪

