No, I gotta get back.

2214
01:31:22,767 --> 01:31:24,400
- [Crow] I've got
a war to fight.

2215
01:31:25,767 --> 01:31:28,733
- Okay, thanks for calling.

2216
01:31:28,733 --> 01:31:29,833
- [Tom] No, thank you.

2217
01:31:31,633 --> 01:31:32,567
- What was it?

2218
01:31:32,567 --> 01:31:33,500
- [Joel] That was my brother.

2219
01:31:33,500 --> 01:31:35,233
Turns out he never died.

2220
01:31:35,233 --> 01:31:36,167
(snickering)

2221
01:31:36,167 --> 01:31:37,633
- I'm sorry.

2222
01:31:37,633 --> 01:31:38,800
- Old Moon Goose came
out with the whole story.

2223
01:31:38,800 --> 01:31:40,067
- [Tom] Muumuus?

2224
01:31:40,067 --> 01:31:41,833
- So things might not
go too bad with them.

2225
01:31:41,833 --> 01:31:42,667
- I hope so.

2226
01:31:44,633 --> 01:31:45,867
- Me too.

2227
01:31:45,867 --> 01:31:47,633
- [Tom] Yeah, we
had a lot of laughs.

2228
01:31:51,567 --> 01:31:53,000
- [Joel] Well, it's been fun.

2229
01:31:56,100 --> 01:31:58,500
- [Crow] Say, I like
the new Barbiemobile.

2230
01:32:05,133 --> 01:32:06,333
- [Tom] Well, I guess that's it.

2231
01:32:06,333 --> 01:32:07,300
Let me know if
you're gonna marry

2232
01:32:07,300 --> 01:32:08,667
another one of my brothers.

2233
01:32:10,500 --> 01:32:11,933
- Give my love to your folks.

2234
01:32:11,933 --> 01:32:14,333
- [Crow] They're dead,
they were killed by bikers.

2235
01:32:14,333 --> 01:32:15,400
- When do you leave?

2236
01:32:15,400 --> 01:32:16,200
- Tomorrow.

2237
01:32:17,567 --> 01:32:19,100
I have to sign some depositions
and things in the morning.

2238
01:32:19,100 --> 01:32:21,767
- [Joel] And they're going
to film every minute of it.

2239
01:32:21,767 --> 01:32:23,733
- [Monte] Mama, be good.

2240
01:32:24,567 --> 01:32:26,133
- [Tom] Be very good.

2241
01:32:26,133 --> 01:32:27,633
- You too, papa.

2242
01:32:27,633 --> 01:32:28,467
- [Joel] Huh?

2243
01:32:29,833 --> 01:32:31,867
- Hey, what are you
gonna do with that thing?

2244
01:32:31,867 --> 01:32:34,200
- [Crow] Thought I'd
make a lamp out of it.

2245
01:32:34,200 --> 01:32:35,667
- Keep it.

2246
01:32:35,667 --> 01:32:36,500
I like it.

2247
01:32:37,600 --> 01:32:39,667
- [Tom] I like this bike.

2248
01:32:41,100 --> 01:32:43,000
(engine rumbling)

2249
01:32:43,000 --> 01:32:44,433
(upbeat music)
- [Joel] Hey.

2250
01:32:44,433 --> 01:32:45,267
Hear that?

2251
01:32:46,500 --> 01:32:47,400
It's the bike song.

2252
01:32:47,400 --> 01:32:49,733
(whistling)

2253
01:32:52,567 --> 01:32:55,000
(dramatic music)

2254
01:32:55,000 --> 01:32:56,267
- [Tom] It was the bike song.

2255
01:32:56,267 --> 01:32:59,000
♪ Into a Hellcats way
of life they lead ♪

2256
01:32:59,000 --> 01:33:01,967
(humming gibberish)

2257
01:33:04,867 --> 01:33:07,533
- [Tom] Wish I had a tambourine.

2258
01:33:08,600 --> 01:33:09,833
Everybody now!

2259
01:33:09,833 --> 01:33:13,200
♪ Hellcats in little
wooly things ♪

2260
01:33:13,200 --> 01:33:14,667
♪ Hellcats ♪

2261
01:33:14,667 --> 01:33:17,667
(singing gibberish)

2262
01:33:18,833 --> 01:33:20,200
♪ Upside down ♪

2263
01:33:20,200 --> 01:33:23,533
♪ When they get in
a dressing gown ♪

2264
01:33:23,533 --> 01:33:24,867
♪ Hellcats ♪

2265
01:33:24,867 --> 01:33:27,000
♪ Wearing Holsted ensembles ♪

2266
01:33:27,000 --> 01:33:28,700
♪ Hellcats ♪

2267
01:33:28,700 --> 01:33:30,633
♪ Losing all their marbles ♪

2268
01:33:30,633 --> 01:33:32,800
♪ Hellcats ♪

2269
01:33:32,800 --> 01:33:34,600
- [Crow] The end.
- [Tom] Okay.

2270
01:33:34,600 --> 01:33:37,533
Oh no, they're gonna
start it over again?

2271
01:33:37,533 --> 01:33:38,733
No, we're not gonna
sit through this twice.

2272
01:33:38,733 --> 01:33:39,600
I'm sorry.

2273
01:33:41,633 --> 01:33:42,800
- [Joel] Let's go.

2274
01:33:42,800 --> 01:33:44,067
- [Tom] Let's
blow, I don't care.

2275
01:33:44,067 --> 01:33:46,533
- [Joel] Ah, lift you up.

2276
01:33:46,533 --> 01:33:48,733
- [Tom] Thank you.

2277
01:33:48,733 --> 01:33:49,900
Groovy music, though.

2278
01:33:49,900 --> 01:33:50,833
(machanical whirring)

2279
01:33:50,833 --> 01:33:53,600
(doors closing)

2280
01:34:01,533 --> 01:34:03,867
- Dear Richard, how are you?

2281
01:34:05,300 --> 01:34:06,133
I am fine.

2282
01:34:07,800 --> 01:34:09,600
Everyone's sad but me.

2283
01:34:10,700 --> 01:34:14,367
Dear Richard, how are you?

2284
01:34:14,367 --> 01:34:16,100
- Whatcha working on, pumpkin?

2285
01:34:16,100 --> 01:34:17,667
- Diary.

2286
01:34:17,667 --> 01:34:20,600
- Oh, she's working
on a diary you guys.

2287
01:34:20,600 --> 01:34:23,333
Hey, honey, you gotta
type into the thing

2288
01:34:23,333 --> 01:34:25,467
for the words to come
out on the paper.

2289
01:34:25,467 --> 01:34:26,533
- Paper.

2290
01:34:26,533 --> 01:34:28,067
- Diary.

2291
01:34:28,067 --> 01:34:29,700
Hey, what do you wanna keep
a diary for, you big femme?

2292
01:34:29,700 --> 01:34:30,900
- Ooh.

2293
01:34:30,900 --> 01:34:32,900
- Yeah, hey, only
ninnies keep diaries.

2294
01:34:32,900 --> 01:34:33,733
- Oooh.

2295
01:34:33,733 --> 01:34:35,300
- Ninny.
- Femme.

2296
01:34:35,300 --> 01:34:36,600
- You guys, that's not fair.

2297
01:34:36,600 --> 01:34:38,000
You know, I keep a diary.

2298
01:34:38,000 --> 01:34:38,833
- Really?
- Diary.

2299
01:34:38,833 --> 01:34:40,333
- Yeah, I do.

2300
01:34:40,333 --> 01:34:43,067
It's a good way to keep from
making mistakes in the future.

2301
01:34:43,067 --> 01:34:44,600
You know, see what
you lived through.

2302
01:34:44,600 --> 01:34:46,833
Kinda like what Neitzsche
says, eternal recurrence.

2303
01:34:46,833 --> 01:34:49,367
- Of the structures and stuff.

2304
01:34:49,367 --> 01:34:52,633
- Ah well, I admit it,
I keep a diary too.

2305
01:34:52,633 --> 01:34:53,833
- Yay!

2306
01:34:53,833 --> 01:34:55,800
- But only of cool stuff
that happened to me.

2307
01:34:55,800 --> 01:34:57,033
- Yeah, me too.

2308
01:34:57,033 --> 01:34:58,300
- Huh?
- What?

2309
01:34:58,300 --> 01:34:59,867
- Me too, okay, I
keep a diary too!

2310
01:34:59,867 --> 01:35:02,367
- All right, come here you guys.

2311
01:35:02,367 --> 01:35:03,733
- Awww!

2312
01:35:03,733 --> 01:35:05,233
- See?

2313
01:35:05,233 --> 01:35:07,367
- Hey Joel, what are you all
of a sudden, Dick Van Patten?

2314
01:35:07,367 --> 01:35:08,567
(laughing)

2315
01:35:08,567 --> 01:35:09,733
- Let's can this corn
and read a letter,

2316
01:35:09,733 --> 01:35:11,767
you big mushwads.
- Letters!

2317
01:35:11,767 --> 01:35:15,900
- All right, this one is to
everyone on the Satellite

2318
01:35:15,900 --> 01:35:18,400
of Love, let's put that
up on still-store, Cambot.

2319
01:35:19,833 --> 01:35:22,667
Thought you might like to know
that you have fans in Italy.

2320
01:35:22,667 --> 01:35:24,200
- Oh.
- Pretty cool.

2321
01:35:24,200 --> 01:35:26,167
- Through the insight and
effort of our friend Chad

2322
01:35:26,167 --> 01:35:29,233
in Dallas, we receive
recordings of MST3K.

2323
01:35:29,233 --> 01:35:31,800
It is a brilliant
switch from Italian TV.

2324
01:35:31,800 --> 01:35:32,967
- I'll say.

2325
01:35:32,967 --> 01:35:34,433
- Some of whose
programs might one day

2326
01:35:34,433 --> 01:35:36,567
be forced upon you
in an experiment.

2327
01:35:36,567 --> 01:35:38,300
- Oh, yikes.

2328
01:35:38,300 --> 01:35:40,400
- If you're ever in the
neighborhood, drop in.

2329
01:35:40,400 --> 01:35:42,733
Arrivederci, Jacqueline McNulty.

2330
01:35:42,733 --> 01:35:45,100
- Linguini.
- Hiroshima, mon amour.

2331
01:35:45,100 --> 01:35:46,933
- Come on you guys, we've
had a pretty good day.

2332
01:35:46,933 --> 01:35:48,133
- Oh, I love you guys.

2333
01:35:48,133 --> 01:35:49,633
- Come here Crow, come here.

2334
01:35:49,633 --> 01:35:51,233
- Ah, ow, ow.

2335
01:35:51,233 --> 01:35:52,867
(crying)

2336
01:35:52,867 --> 01:35:55,567
- I think I am going to vomit.

2337
01:35:55,567 --> 01:35:57,500
That is the most
disgusting display

2338
01:35:57,500 --> 01:35:59,433
of emotion I have ever seen.

2339
01:35:59,433 --> 01:36:02,033
Get us out of this
nightmare, Frank.

2340
01:36:02,033 --> 01:36:04,133
(crying)

2341
01:36:06,233 --> 01:36:07,933
- Oh the pathos.

2342
01:36:07,933 --> 01:36:08,767
The joy.

2343
01:36:10,733 --> 01:36:13,567
Why can't we know love
the way they know love!?

2344
01:36:13,567 --> 01:36:15,933
- Would you push
the button please?

2345
01:36:19,900 --> 01:36:21,500
- Come on, give me a
hug you big galoot.

2346
01:36:21,500 --> 01:36:23,033
- Would you get away from me?

2347
01:36:23,033 --> 01:36:26,733
- Come on, work the steps
Doctor, give me a big hug.

2348
01:36:26,733 --> 01:36:28,200
- You know, Frank...

2349
01:36:29,200 --> 01:36:30,533
Now you've got me doing it.

2350
01:36:32,133 --> 01:36:33,900
- What's so bad
about feeling good?

2351
01:36:33,900 --> 01:36:36,033
(crying)

2352
01:36:36,033 --> 01:36:38,233
- Let's push the
button together.

2353
01:36:38,233 --> 01:36:41,133
(slow theme music)

2354
01:37:43,833 --> 01:37:46,900
(shouting gibberish)

